      <li>
      Create a secret to store your Azure credentials in by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create secret generic <secret_name> --from-literal=<azure_secret_access_key_name>=<azure_secret_access_key_value> \\\n    -n my-issuer-namespace"} lang="terminal" />
      <ul>
      <li>Replace <code>&lt;secret_name&gt;</code> with your secret name.</li>
      <li>Replace <code>&lt;azure_secret_access_key_name&gt;</code> with your Azure secret access key name.</li>
      <li>Replace <code>&lt;azure_secret_access_key_value&gt;</code> with your Azure secret key.</li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create an issuer:
      <ol>
      <li>
      Create a YAML file, for example, <code>issuer.yaml</code>, that defines the <code>Issuer</code> object:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: cert-manager.io/v1\nkind: Issuer\nmetadata:\n  name: <acme-dns01-azuredns-issuer>\n  namespace: <issuer_namespace>\nspec:\n  acme:\n    preferredChain: \"\"\n    privateKeySecretRef:\n      name: <secret_private_key>\n    server: <server>\n    solvers:\n    - dns01:\n        azureDNS:\n          clientID: <azure_client_id>\n          clientSecretSecretRef:\n            name: <secret_name>\n            key: <azure_secret_access_key_name>\n          subscriptionID: <azure_subscription_id>\n          tenantID: <azure_tenant_id>\n          resourceGroupName: <azure_dns_zone_resource_group>\n          hostedZoneName: <azure_dns_zone>\n          environment: AzurePublicCloud"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;acme-dns01-azuredns-issuer&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies a name for the issuer.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;issuer_namespace&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies your issuer namespace.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;secret_private_key&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the name of the secret to store the ACME account private key in.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;server&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the URL to access the ACME server’s <code>directory</code> endpoint. This example uses the <em>Let’s Encrypt</em> staging environment.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;azure_client_id&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies your Azure client ID.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;secret_name&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies a name of the client secret.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;azure_secret_access_key_name&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the client secret key name.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;azure_subscription_id&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies your Azure subscription ID.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;azure_tenant_id&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies your Azure tenant ID.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;azure_dns_zone_resource_group&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the name of the Azure DNS zone resource group.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;azure_dns_zone&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the name of Azure DNS zone.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the <code>Issuer</code> object by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create -f issuer.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      </li>
      </ol>
